LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Queering Art History Tour
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the IU LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, join us fo
 r a tour of the Eskenazi Museum of Art's collection viewed through a quee
 r lens. Participants can expect to learn about queer artists and works of
  art and also share their own perspectives on the collection.&#160\;  Thi
 s tour group will meet before 5:30 p.m. in the Eskenazi Museum atrium and
  will be led by the Museum's Arts-Based Wellness Experiences Manager\, Ke
 aton Evans-Black.  If interested in attending\, please RSVP by clicking t
 he "Register" button below.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In partnership with the IU LGBTQ+ Cultu
 re Center\, join us for a tour of the Eskenazi Museum of Art's collection
  viewed through a queer lens. Participants can expect to learn about quee
 r artists and works of art and also share their own perspectives on the c
 ollection.&#160\;</p><p>  This tour group will meet before 5:30 p.m. in t
 he Eskenazi Museum atrium and will be led by the Museum's Arts-Based Well
 ness Experiences Manager\, Keaton Evans-Black.</p><p>  If interested in a
 ttending\, please RSVP by clicking the "Register" button below.</p>
